ukberi-tibyan:53-53.t:
Allah the Exalted said: {قَالُوا يَا هود مَا جئتنا بِبَيِّنَة وَمَا نَحن بتاركي آلِهَتنَا عَن قَوْلك وَمَا نَحن لَك بمؤمنين}
His saying (مَا جِئْتَنَا بِبَيِّنَةٍ): the bāʾ may be attached (mutaʿalliq) to جِئْتَ, the implied form being "you have not shown a clear proof".
It may also be a ḥāl (circumstantial), i.e. "while you have with you a clear proof", or "arguing with a clear proof".
